============================================================================
A. Fast-MCD on the full pool: genuine failure, or a search artefact?
============================================================================
N=250, p=4, h=127.  Contaminants sit at squared Mahalanobis
distance 48 from the centre (clean E[D]=4) with scatter
0.5 I, so they form a TIGHT, well separated cluster.

--- eps=0.20   outliers ~50 < h=127 ---
                   method     RMSE   median      P90   frac>1
         sklearn Fast-MCD    0.357    0.129    0.233    0.035
          50-start C-step    0.142    0.122    0.201    0.000
              sample mean    1.230    1.208    1.432    0.895
  determinant diagnostic (50-start search):
    returned subset has SMALLER logdet than the all-clean subset in 92% of runs

--- eps=0.30   outliers ~75 < h=127 ---
                   method     RMSE   median      P90   frac>1
         sklearn Fast-MCD    1.978    2.027    2.334    0.900
          50-start C-step    1.312    0.172    2.456    0.305
              sample mean    1.808    1.805    2.008    1.000
  determinant diagnostic (50-start search):
    returned subset has SMALLER logdet than the all-clean subset in 82% of runs
    among the 30% of runs with squared error > 1, that figure is 100%, mean logdet gap 0.272
    => the objective PREFERS the contaminated subset; this is estimator breakdown, not a search failure.


